+++ b/docs/alibabacloud.md
@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+# Alibaba Cloud ESSD
+
+This provider implements the existing block-volume and cloud-recovery interfaces.
+CAA must also support Alibaba disk attachment and guest disk-ID discovery.
+ESSD PL0 volumes support create, lookup, recovery and delete; expansion, snapshots
+and clones are not implemented.
+
+Use `provider=alibabacloud` with `alibabacloud.region`, `zoneId` and `clusterId`.
+The disk zone must match the PodVM zone. Cluster and driver tags scope recovery.
+The combined upstream DaemonSet retains its node-local volume store. Startup
+rebuilds completed records through ListManagedVolumes; no state PVC is required.
+CreateDisk uses a stable cluster/volume ClientToken, without a separate journal.
+
+For ACK RRSA, set `alibabacloud.rrsa.enabled=true`, `roleArn` and `oidcProviderArn`.
+Trust the chart's ServiceAccount in namespace caa-csi-block with audience
+sts.aliyuncs.com. The driver receives a projected token; both controller and node
+RPCs use that identity. Alternatively provide `alibabacloud.credentialsSecret`
+with SDK credential environment variables. Do not enable both methods.
+
+Required cloud actions are ecs:CreateDisk, ecs:DescribeDisks and ecs:DeleteDisk.
+Scope permissions and tags to the deployment. Keep the same cluster ID and
+bootstrap region/zone when recovering records. Cloud recovery reconstructs
+completed volumes, not arbitrary pending requests or all historical parameters.
+
+Helm is the normal install path. The new Alibaba files under deploy/ show the
+same DaemonSet, bootstrap ConfigMap and StorageClass; combine them with the
+upstream namespace, ServiceAccount, RBAC and CSIDriver resources. Replace the
+uppercase sample values and image digest before applying them.
